# L4 Milestone List

`memory-bank/active/milestones.md` is the L4 project's plan and state tracker. It serves two purposes simultaneously:

1. **In-flight signal**: its presence tells `/niko` that an L4 project is active, triggering milestone transition routing instead of normal state handling.
2. **State tracker**: the checklist records which milestones are complete and which remain.

Narrative requirements and most of the definition of done live in `memory-bank/active/projectbrief.md`. This file is sequencing plus enough for a later worker to understand the document after `/niko` Step 2a deletes `tasks.md` and `progress.md`.

## File Format

```markdown
# Milestones: <task-id>

## Cross-milestone invariants & constraints

[properties no milestone may violate. When two milestones share an artifact, state the handoff rule: who may touch it, and when.]

## Execution Order

[optional Mermaid flowchart of dependency relationships - omit if all milestones are sequential]

- [ ] <Milestone 1: one-line deliverable, optional existing ticket>
- [ ] <Milestone 2: one-line deliverable, optional existing ticket>
- [ ] <Milestone 3: one-line deliverable, optional existing ticket>

## Per-milestone done and risks

| Milestone | Done | Risks / invariants | Ref |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| <exact checkbox text> | judgeable done | critical risks, or see invariants | ticket URL, or projectbrief pointer |
```

Rules:
- Header must be `# Milestones: <task-id>` where `task-id` matches the active task's ID in `memory-bank/active/tasks.md`
- Each milestone is a standard GFM checkbox: `- [ ]` (unchecked) or `- [x]` (complete)
- One milestone per line — no sub-bullets, no TDD steps, no file lists on the checkbox line
- An existing ticket id or URL may be part of that one line. Do not create tickets. Do not add a second sentence of notes on the checkbox line
- Description is a single line: concise, action-oriented, specific enough that a future agent can classify it as L1/L2/L3 together with its done/risks/ref row and the memory bank
- Only the real checklist may use `- [ ]` / `- [x]`. Sections (invariants, DAG, done/risks table or headings) must not contain checkboxes — complexity analysis identifies milestones by those markers only
- The optional dependency flowchart (if present) lives under Execution Order and is not a milestone
- Heading blocks keyed to checkbox text may replace the table. They still must not use checklist markers

## What Makes a Good Milestone

Each milestone must satisfy all of these:

- **Independently deliverable** - can be planned, built, tested, and committed as a self-contained sub-run with no dependency on future milestones
- **L1/L2/L3 scoped** - small enough to pass through the complexity analysis decision tree without itself being classified L4
- **Concrete** - the description names what is being built, not the activity ("Add user authentication flow" not "Work on auth")
- **Non-overlapping** - milestones cover distinct ground; no two milestones should touch the same files for the same purpose
- **Judgeable done** - the done/risks row (or a covering cross-milestone invariant) states what shipped looks like and what must not be lost
- **Task-description ref** - an existing ticket if one exists, otherwise a pointer into `projectbrief.md`

If a milestone fails any of these criteria during preflight, it should be split, merged, or rewritten before sub-runs begin.

## Lifecycle

| Event | Who | Action |
|-------|-----|--------|
| L4 Plan phase | `.cursor/skills/shared/niko/references/level4/level4-plan.md` | Creates `memory-bank/active/milestones.md` |
| `/niko` re-entry - sub-run complete | `/niko` Step 2a (Advance L4 Milestone) | Checks off the completed milestone (`- [ ]` → `- [x]`) |
| `/niko` re-entry - unchecked remain | `/niko` Step 2a → Step 7 (Classify) | Classifies first unchecked as L1/L2/L3, initiates sub-run |
| `/niko` re-entry - all `- [x]` | `/niko` Step 2a | Routes to capstone archive |
| Capstone archive | `.cursor/skills/shared/niko/references/level4/level4-archive.md` | Deletes `memory-bank/active/milestones.md` |

🚨 **Do not create or modify `memory-bank/active/milestones.md` outside of these lifecycle events.** Its presence is used as a binary signal by `/niko` — creating it manually will cause `/niko` to enter L4 milestone transition routing on the next invocation.
